<Base title="Free Island privacy" description="Privacy policy for Free Island, the Android camera island app.">
  <div class="prose">
    <h1>Free Island privacy policy</h1>
    <p class="lede">Free Island is an Android app made by Abhinav Bansal. It does not collect, store, sell or share any personal data. The app has no internet permission, so it cannot send anything off your phone.</p>

    <h2>What the app reads, and why</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Notifications (notification access):</strong> to show notifications, calls, timers, music, navigation and downloads in the island, the app reads notifications as they arrive: the app name, title, text, icon, picture and buttons. It uses them only to draw the island at that moment and does not save them.</li>
      <li><strong>Accessibility service:</strong> the app uses Android's accessibility service to draw the island over the status bar. It also reads the name of the app that is open, so it can hide the island in apps you choose. It does not read what is on screen, what you type or your passwords.</li>
      <li><strong>Media sessions:</strong> to show what is playing, the app reads the track title, artist, album art and playback position from the music or video app.</li>
      <li><strong>Bluetooth (optional):</strong> if you allow it, the app reads the name and battery level of Bluetooth headphones when they connect, to show them in the island.</li>
      <li><strong>Installed apps:</strong> the app lists the apps on your phone that have a launcher icon, so you can pick shortcuts and choose apps where the island hides or never pops up.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>What the app stores</h2>
    <p>Only your settings (sizes, colours, switches and the apps you picked) are stored, on your phone. Uninstalling the app deletes them.</p>

    <h2>Sharing</h2>
    <p>Nothing is shared with anyone. The app has no ads, no analytics, no crash reporting and no account.</p>

    <h2>Children</h2>
    <p>Free Island is not directed at children under 13.</p>

    <h2>Changes and contact</h2>
    <p>If this policy changes, the new version will be posted at this address with a new date. Questions: <a href="mailto:abhibansal60@gmail.com">abhibansal60@gmail.com</a>.</p>

    <p class="meta">Last updated 24 October 2026.</p>
  </div>
</Base>
